              {
                "insert": "JudgeAdvisory",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            "Reading a justification against a hunk is judgment. Jev returns a native probability that code can threshold at 0.85."
          ],
          [
            "Continue or stop",
            [
              {
                "insert": "Decision node "
              },
              {
                "insert": "ContinueOrStop",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            "Whether a new strategy can close a 97.4% match is judgment. Today a fixed counter makes this call."
          ],
          [
            "Low-confidence escalation",
            [
              {
                "insert": "Call "
              },
              {
                "insert": "JudgeAdvisoryWithRationale",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": ", then a human"
              }
            ],
            "A p between 0.4 and 0.85 is too unsure to act on. The BAML judge adds a rationale. Its confidence is self-reported, so code does not threshold it."
          ],
          [
            "Abstained",
            "Code routes it, a human or the budget decides",
            "Abstained is a normal result, not an error. An advisory goes to the operator review queue. A ContinueOrStop abstain falls back to the attempt budget counter."
          ]
        ]
      },
